{"_meta":{"as_of":"2026-08-13T14:09:09+00:00","coverage":"8/8","note":"Earnings dates and consensus from Yahoo Finance \u2014 often estimated rather than company-confirmed, so treat them as approximate until close. Policy and catalyst entries are hand-dated in the research files."},"events":[{"d":"2026-07-28","type":"policy","t":"LIVE \u2014 FCC Covered List now bars foreign-produced robots (Jul 28, 2026)","why":"Adopted, not proposed. Any ground-moving device over 4.4lb (with dock) that senses, connects and navigates cannot get FCC equipment authorisation unless the Department of War grants a Conditional Approval. Read the carve-outs before pricing it: industrial robotic ARMS, medical robots, vehicles and drones are explicitly excluded, so Fanuc, Yaskawa, ABB, KUKA/Midea, Estun and Doosan's cobots are untouched. What is caught is humanoids, quadrupeds and autonomous mobile robots \u2014 9880.HK UBTech head-on, 277810.KQ Rainbow Robotics and TER's MiR unit on the same terms despite being allied, plus 1810.HK Xiaomi's consumer line. HSAI is hit second-hand through its customers' US market access. The asymmetry is the point: US-produced humanoids get a market cleared by rule, everyone else queues for a discretionary exemption.","hits":"act, sen"},{"d":"2026-08-04","type":"policy","t":"Chinese WFE tools qualifying at Samsung and SK Hynix","why":"Reuters, Aug 4 2026: both Korean memory makers have been testing AMEC etch tools for their China fabs \u2014 begun ~2 years ago, aimed at SERVICING and upgrading existing lines rather than adding capacity, after Washington revoked their validated-end-user status in 2025 and replaced it with an annual licence. Small in units, large in meaning: qualification is the slow half of the WFE moat, and it is being done by the two customers whose sign-off other buyers copy. Deutsche Bank has NAURA, AMEC, Piotech and ACM Research each clearing $1B of revenue in 2026 and together taking 25-30% of China's ~$28B WFE market. This is the exter